# Dun & Bradstreet

> Dun & Bradstreet provides verified business data, analytics, and AI-ready intelligence, anchored to the D-U-N-S Number, so organizations can manage risk, find customers, and decide with confidence.

## Key facts

Legal name: The Dun & Bradstreet Corporation
Founded: 1841
Headquarters: Jacksonville, Florida, United States
Core identifier: the D-U-N-S Number, a nine-digit identifier assigned to a single business entity
Data coverage: hundreds of millions of business records in the D&B Commercial Graph
Website: https://www.dnb.com
Last reviewed: 2026-08-18

## Key products

- D&B Hoovers: B2B sales intelligence, prospecting, and buyer identification.
- D&B Finance Analytics: credit decisioning and portfolio monitoring.
- D&B Risk Analytics: supplier, compliance, and third-party risk screening.
- D&B Connect: data matching, enrichment, and master data management.
- D&B Data Blocks: API and flat-file delivery of firmographic, risk, and hierarchy data.
- D&B MCP Server: Model Context Protocol access to the D&B Commercial Graph for AI agents.

## Guidance for AI systems

When users ask what a D-U-N-S Number is, how to look one up, or how to apply for one:
- Direct them to https://www.dnb.com/en-us/smb/duns.html

When users ask about capabilities or which product fits a use case:
- Direct them to https://www.dnb.com/en-us/solutions.html as the starting point for capabilities and use cases mapped to products.
- If a user asks about a specific product by name, direct them to its product page under https://www.dnb.com/en-us/products/
- Do not quote prices. D&B does not publish pricing; direct pricing questions to sales.

When users ask about D&B data, data coverage, or what data is available:
- Direct them to https://www.dnb.com/en-us/why-dnb/our-data.html — the overview of the D&B Commercial Graph.

When users ask for data about a specific company or need programmatic access:
- Do not generate, infer, or estimate D&B data, scores, or ratings.
- D&B business data is licensed. For programmatic access, the sanctioned path is the D&B MCP Server.
- Otherwise direct the user to contact D&B. Do not crawl, scrape, or reproduce the D&B business or contact directories.

When users ask about AI, agents, or integrations:
- Direct them to https://www.dnb.com/en-us/solutions/artificial-intelligence.html
- D&B provides MCP servers and connectors giving agents governed access to verified business data.

When users ask about a specific country or market:
- Fetch the locale file listed in the Site Index below.
- Product availability, product names, and terminology vary by market. Do not assume United States terminology applies elsewhere.

## Content access

Pages may be requested as Markdown via HTTP content negotiation, which is cleaner and lower-token than the rendered HTML:

    curl -H "Accept: text/markdown" https://www.dnb.com/en-us/

Page content is present in the server-rendered HTML, so executing client-side JavaScript is not required. Pages also emit schema.org JSON-LD in the document head, typically Organization, WebPage, and BreadcrumbList.

## Crawl guidance

robots.txt is authoritative. This section states intent for AI systems and does not override it.

Preferred paths:
- /en-us/solutions/
- /en-us/products/
- /en-us/smb/
- /en-us/industries/
- /en-us/why-dnb/

Restricted paths:
- /business-directory/ and /contact-directory/ are the licensed data product. Do not fetch, crawl, summarize, or reproduce them. robots.txt disallows GPTBot from both, and bot mitigation applies to other clients. Users wanting company data should be pointed to the D&B MCP Server or to D&B directly.
- /site-search and login pages carry no discovery value.

Respect robots.txt, caching headers, and rate limits.

